# Terraform Provider for Docker Compose

[![Tests](https://github.com/rambhiad/terraform-provider-docker-compose/actions/workflows/test.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/rambhiad/terraform-provider-docker-compose/actions/workflows/test.yml)
[![Release](https://github.com/rambhiad/terraform-provider-docker-compose/actions/workflows/release.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/rambhiad/terraform-provider-docker-compose/actions/workflows/release.yml)

Terraform provider for managing Docker Compose projects on remote hosts via SSH.

## Features

- Manage Docker Compose projects on remote hosts
- SSH-based remote execution with private key authentication
- Support for custom compose files and project directories
- Automatic cleanup on resource destruction

## Requirements

- [Terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/downloads) >= 1.0
- [Go](https://golang.org/doc/install) >= 1.23
- Remote host with Docker Compose installed
- SSH access to remote host

## Installation

```hcl
terraform {
  required_providers {
    docker-compose = {
      source = "rambhiad/docker-compose"
    }
  }
}
```

## Usage

```hcl
provider "docker-compose" {
  host        = "remote-host.example.com"
  user        = "deploy"
  private_key = file("~/.ssh/id_rsa")
}

resource "docker-compose_project" "app" {
  name             = "myapp"
  compose_file     = file("docker-compose.yml")
  directory        = "/opt/myapp"
  remove_orphans   = true
  remove_volumes   = true
}
```

## Documentation

Full documentation is available in the [docs](./docs) directory.

## Development

### Building

```shell
make build
```

### Testing

```shell
make test
```

### Generating Documentation

```shell
make gen
```

